# conf/fleet-env-internal.list — FLEET_* names the scripts read that are NOT
# settings (issue #1101). bin/conf-surface-selftest.sh holds bin/ to: every
# ${FLEET_X:-…} a script reads is either a key in fleet.conf.example (any @tier,
# including internal) or listed here — so an undocumented knob cannot quietly
# join the config surface again. One name per line, then its kind and a reason:
#   handoff  env one fleet process sets for another (never in a conf)
#   seam     a test-injection point (fake command, fixed clock, sandbox path)
#   path     a state/log/cache location override
#   knob     a hand-override tuning value with a safe in-code default
#   alias    a retired twin of a documented key, still read for old confs
#   legacy / doc  see the reason
# Adding a line here is a decision: a knob an operator would plausibly change
# belongs in fleet.conf.example (with a tag line) instead.

FLEET_ACCOUNT_ADD_CLAUDE_BIN       seam: the claude binary `fleet account add` runs for `setup-token` (#2084)
FLEET_ACCOUNT_ADD_CODEX_BIN        seam: the codex binary `fleet account add` runs for `login` (#2084)
FLEET_ACCOUNT_LABEL                handoff: the Claude account label a launch was assigned
FLEET_ACCOUNT_PAUSED_CMD           seam: prints the hub client-settings JSON instead of curl (fleet-account.sh quota_paused_fetch, #2083)
FLEET_ACCOUNT_PHASE_WINDOW         knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-account.sh)
FLEET_ACCOUNT_SELECTED             handoff: the account pick already ran for this launch
FLEET_ACCOUNT_TARGET               handoff: the account a migrate/move relaunches on
FLEET_ADMIT_OWNER                  handoff: whose admission reservation this process holds (default $$; fleet_admit_*, #2502)
FLEET_ALERTS_ALLCAPPED_SECS        knob: how long an `accounts · all capped` stamp stays an alert (fleet-alerts.sh, 900)
FLEET_ALERTS_EVENT_DEDUP           knob: same kind + text within this many seconds is one alerts event (fleet-alerts.sh event, 60)
FLEET_ALERTS_EVENT_KEEP            knob: how long alerts.events keeps a background event (fleet-alerts.sh, 2592000 = 30 days)
FLEET_ALERTS_EVENT_LIVE            knob: how long a background event counts as a ▲ row before it is popup history (fleet-alerts.sh, 3600)
FLEET_ALERTS_HISTORY_ROWS          knob: how many past events the alerts popup lists (fleet-alerts.sh, 100)
FLEET_ALERTS_HUB_FLASH_SECS        knob: hub unreachable this long before the one hub-lost flash (fleet-alerts.sh, 300)
FLEET_ALERTS_DISK                  seam: 0 skips the alerts producer's own df (a selftest that counts df calls)
FLEET_ALERTS_LOAD_PCT              knob: load per core ×100 at which `machine · load high` is raised (fleet-alerts.sh, 80, #1616)
FLEET_ALERTS_MACHINE               knob: 0 turns off the machine load / memory alerts (fleet-alerts.sh, #1616; selftests set it)
FLEET_ALERTS_SERVICES              knob: 0 turns off the registered-service alerts (fleet-alerts.sh `service · failed`, #2526)
FLEET_ALERTS_MEM_PCT               knob: used-memory % at which `machine · memory high` is raised (fleet-alerts.sh, 85, #1616)
FLEET_ALERTS_MUTE_SECS             knob: how long `m` in the alerts popup mutes a row (fleet-alerts.sh, 3600)
FLEET_ALERTS_REAUTH_SECS           knob: how old the account.reauth stamp may be before the bar refreshes it through `.fleet-account.py logins` (fleet-alerts.sh, 60)
FLEET_ALERTS_STALL_TTL             knob: how long a forgotten `stalled` alert outlives its killed waiter (fleet-alerts.sh, 21600)
FLEET_ALERTS_TRACE                 knob: how long a cleared alert keeps its ↻ row (fleet-alerts.sh, 1800)
FLEET_ALERTS_TTL                   knob: status-bar refresh interval of alerts.ndjson (fleet-alerts.sh, 5; 0 = every render)
FLEET_ANSWER_POLL                  knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-answer.sh)
FLEET_ANSWER_TIMEOUT               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-answer.sh)
FLEET_ANSWER_HUB_WAIT              knob: seconds fleet-answer.sh waits for a worker_answer on another machine to settle (fleet-answer.sh, 90, #2729)
FLEET_AUTO_RESTORE                 knob: 0 turns off the diskguard tick's fleet-restore.sh --auto pull-up (issue #1784, default on)
FLEET_AUTO_RESTORE_MAX_AGE         knob: --auto skips a fleet whose restore map is older than this many seconds (fleet-restore.sh, 86400)
FLEET_AWAIT_ARMED                  handoff: fleet-await re-exec guard (alarm armed once)
FLEET_AWAIT_CPU_PCT                knob: % of a core above which a `working` child counts as busy, not stalled (fleet-await.sh, 10)
FLEET_AWAIT_TICK                   knob: seconds between ledger-file checks while waiting; a change reads at once (fleet-await.sh, 1, #1272)
FLEET_BASE_DEPS_LOG                path: state/log location override (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_BASE_DEPS_RETRY_BASE         knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_BASE_DEPS_RETRY_CAP          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_BASE_SYNC                    knob: per-repo 0 opts a repo out of base-branch sync
FLEET_BASE_SYNC_LEASE_TTL          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-base-sync.sh)
FLEET_BG_SOCK                      handoff: the background peer socket a message is sent over
FLEET_BOOTSTRAP_GIT_BASE           seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-login-bootstrap.sh)
FLEET_BOOTSTRAP_CACHE              path: the machine cache a new login installs from; `off` = none (fleet-bootstrap-cache.sh, issue #2297)
FLEET_BOOT_ID_CMD                  seam: a fake boot-session id for the diskguard crash harvest (fleet-diskguard.sh, #1294)
FLEET_BREW_LOG                     path: the brew-perms repair log (fleet-brew-perms.sh, #2283)
FLEET_BREW_LOGINS                  seam: how many logins the machine has (fleet-brew-perms.sh, #2283)
FLEET_BREW_ME                      seam: who this login is for the prefix-owner check (fleet-brew-perms.sh, #2283)
FLEET_BREW_PREFIX                  seam: the Homebrew prefix, a sandbox in the drill (fleet-brew-perms.sh, #2283)
FLEET_C                            path: the dash cache root ($TMPDIR/.claude-dash) — tests point it at a sandbox
FLEET_CC_PROJECTS_DIR              path: state/log location override (fleet-migrate.sh)
FLEET_CC_SESSIONS_DIR              path: state/log location override (fleet-lib.sh)
FLEET_CLAUDE_BIN                   path: the claude binary fleet_find_tool tries first (issue #1774)
FLEET_CLAUDE_COMM                  seam: the process name pane scans treat as Claude
FLEET_CLAUDE_INSTALL_CMD           seam: the Claude Code installer command (fleet-login-bootstrap.sh) — tests swap in a stub
FLEET_CLAUDE_TMP_ROOT              seam: the Claude scratchpad root the listener sweep anchors on (selftest sandbox)
FLEET_CLIENT_ACTIONS               knob: 0 = the shell starts no action loop — nothing a session asks to show you opens here (fleet-shell.sh actions, 1, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_ACTIONS_CONNECT       seam: what opens an ssh master to a machine for a forward / a fetch (default python3 fleet-connect.py; the selftest's fake, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_ACTIONS_IDLE          knob: seconds the action loop sleeps when it has no lease or no hub (fleet-client-actions.py, 3, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_PASTE_OS               test seam: the OS fleet-shell.sh paste_sed decides ⌃V by (uname -s; fleet-client-upload-selftest.sh, #2757)
FLEET_CLIENT_ACTIONS_POLL          seam: one poll answer instead of the hub (fleet-client-actions-selftest.sh, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_DIR                   path: the shell's state dir the action loop reads (lease, key, where; fleet-shell.sh sets it, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_DOWNLOADS             seam: where a shown file lands instead of ~/Downloads (fleet-client-actions-selftest.sh, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_ESCAPE_CMD            seam: what writes a raw escape to the client in use (default fleet-client-escape.sh, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_FLEET_OPEN            seam: fleet-open.sh as the action loop runs it for an iTerm2 at the far end of an ssh (#1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_FLEET_SHOW            seam: fleet-show.sh as the action loop runs it for an iTerm2 at the far end of an ssh (#1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_KEY_FILE              path: the lease's action key, 0600 (fleet-shell.sh sets it; fleet-client-lease.py writes, fleet-client-actions.py reads, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_LEASE_CMD             seam: the client-lease command fleet-shell.sh asks (default python3 fleet-client-lease.py; fleet-client-lease-selftest.sh swaps in a fake hub, #1715)
FLEET_CLIENT_LEASE_EVERY           knob: seconds between the shell keeper's client-lease renewals (fleet-shell.sh keeper, 15, #1715)
FLEET_CERT_CHECK_EVERY             knob: seconds between the shell keeper's certificate checks (fleet-shell.sh keeper, 300, #2112)
FLEET_CERT_RENEW_UNDER             knob: renew the connection certificate when less than this many seconds are left (fleet-shell.sh keeper, 3600, #2112)
FLEET_CERT_RENEW_CMD               test seam: the keeper's certificate renewal command (fleet-shell.sh keeper → fleet-login.py renew, #2112)
FLEET_CLIENT_INPUT_EVERY           knob: seconds between the shell keeper's looks at its clients' last input (fleet-shell.sh keeper, 5, #1932)
FLEET_CLIENT_LIST_FILE             path: the person's clients as the hub last said (fleet-shell.sh sets it; fleet-client-lease.py writes, the top line reads, #1932)
FLEET_CLIENT_NOTIFY_CMD            seam: the system notifier the action loop runs (default osascript / notify-send, #1717)
FLEET_NOTIFY_SEND_CMD              seam: what fleet_notify.py hands an event to (default fleet-client-actions.py notify, #2759)
FLEET_NOTIFY_BARK_CMD              seam: the phone push (the address on stdin; default a GET to the Bark URL, #2759)
FLEET_NOTIFY_OPEN_CMD              seam: a notification click's terminal when none is attached (default iTerm2 via osascript, #2759)
FLEET_NOTIFY_LOG                   path: logs/notify.ndjson override (#2759)
FLEET_NOTIFY_DONE_MERGE            knob: one batch's dones within this many seconds are one notification (600, #2759)
FLEET_NOTIFY_SOUND                 handoff: 1 when the notifier seam should sound (fleet-client-actions.py → FLEET_CLIENT_NOTIFY_CMD, #2759)
FLEET_CLIENT_OPEN_CMD              seam: the opener the action loop runs (default open / xdg-open, #1717)
FLEET_CLIENT_TTY                   seam: the terminal fleet-client-lease.py asks XTVERSION on (default /dev/tty; fleet-client-where-selftest.sh hands it a pty, #1716)
FLEET_CLIENT_BADGE_CACHE           path: where fleet-client-badge.sh keeps its last where read (~/.cache/claude-fleet/shell/tmp, #1779)
FLEET_CLIENT_BADGE_LOGIN           seam: the login the status-bar badge shows instead of the certificate's principal (fleet-client-badge.sh, #2365)
FLEET_CLOCK_POLL                   knob: how often fleet-onboard-clock.sh reads its terminal (0.25 s, #2267)
FLEET_CLOCK_SSH_SHIM               seam: a dir put first on the clock sandbox's PATH — a fake node's ssh / hostname (newcomer-e2e clock step, #2267)
FLEET_CLOCK_STEP_SECS              knob: fleet-onboard-clock.sh's deadline per wait (180 s; a run gets 3×, #2267)
FLEET_COMPOSE_LOG                  path: the writing area's usage log, logs/compose.ndjson (issue #1955)
FLEET_DIST_SOURCE                  knob: `github` = the one-version fallback to fetching versions from GitHub (EPIC #2770 C3); fleet doctor's dist row WARNs on it (fleet-dist-source.sh, #2776)
FLEET_CCQUOTA                      path: the ccquota that checks the hub's release (default PATH, then ~/.local/bin — fleet-release-lib.sh, #2773; selftests point it at a fake)
FLEET_RELEASE_KEY_TIMEOUT          knob: internal pacing, seconds fleet-release-key.sh waits for the hub's /v1/fleet/release/key (default 10, #2773)
FLEET_ORPHAN_ALL_USERS             handoff: fleet-node-supervisor.py sets it on its root orphan watchdog task (every login's orphans, #2331)
FLEET_DRILL_INSTALL_INVITE         handoff: an invite code for the clock's /i/<code> line, never an argv (fleet-onboard-clock.sh, #2267)
FLEET_PLACE_TIMING                 handoff: where fleet-client-place.sh writes a done start's node timing points, set by fleet-compose.py (issue #2238)
FLEET_PUBLISH_AUDIENCE             knob: the OIDC audience fleet-release-publish.sh asks the Actions runtime for (default ccquota-fleet-release, the hub's CCQUOTA_FLEET_PUBLISH_AUDIENCE — #2772)
FLEET_PUBLISH_TOKEN                env handoff: the hub's publish-only fallback bearer for fleet-release-publish.sh outside Actions (a secret; never a file or argv — #2772)
FLEET_REMOTE_GONE_SECS             knob: how long a proxy pane waits for a session not live on its machine (restart) before saying it is gone (fleet-remote-view.sh, #2484)
FLEET_REMOTE_GONE_STEP             knob: seconds between those asks (fleet-remote-view.sh, #2484)
FLEET_SESSIONS_STATE_CMD           seam: prints OPEN/CLOSED for <repo> <issue> instead of fleet-gh.sh (fleet-sessions-snapshot.sh restore, #2484)
FLEET_STABLE_PUBLISH_WORKFLOW      knob: the workflow fleet-stable.sh move dispatches after a move by hand to hand the hub the new stable (default stable-publish.yml, #2772)
FLEET_START_WARM                   knob: 0 = a start never takes a warm-pool window; always the cold path (fleet-control-read.sh, 1, #2234)
FLEET_STATE_PRIMARY_SECS           knob: how long the agent's OSC 7501 report holds the hooks and guessers off (120; read from the env by hooks, #2537)
FLEET_STEWARD_QUOTA_CMD            seam: replaces `fleet-quotawatch.sh --status` in fleet-steward-conflicts.sh (its selftest, #2673)
FLEET_STEWARD_FILES_BUDGET         knob: at most this many REST /pulls/N/files reads a run of fleet-steward-conflicts.sh (10, #2673)
FLEET_STEWARD_FILES_TTL            knob: seconds a PR's cached file list holds before fleet-steward-conflicts.sh rereads it (900, #2673)
FLEET_STEWARD_CI_STUCK             knob: seconds past which a queued run counts as stuck, not waiting (fleet-steward-conflicts.sh, 86400, #2673)
FLEET_SUBMIT_WAIT_SECS             knob: seconds the first turn waits for an idle, empty input before giving up (fleet-pane-submit.sh, 5, #2234)
FLEET_SUBMIT_CONFIRM_SECS          knob: seconds the first turn is watched after its Enter, re-pressing Enter while the text sits in the box (fleet-pane-submit.sh, 6, #2430)
FLEET_CODEX_SEED_CONFIRM           knob: 0 = never press Enter for a Codex seed left in the composer (fleet-codex-seed.py, on, #2430)
FLEET_CODEX_SEED_SECS              knob: seconds a Codex launch watches its composer for the unsent seed (fleet-codex-seed.py, 30, #2430)
FLEET_CODEX_SEED_TICK              test seam: the seed watcher's poll interval when run standalone (fleet-codex-seed.py, 1 s, #2430)
FLEET_BACKFILL_TRIES               knob: how many times a warm start's paperwork tries to file / bind its issue (fleet-start-backfill.sh, 3, #2235)
FLEET_BACKFILL_RETRY_SECS          knob: seconds between those tries (fleet-start-backfill.sh, 10, #2235)
FLEET_CONTROL_OP                   handoff: the start's operation id, fleet_control.py → fleet-control-read.sh → fleet-start-backfill.sh, which stamps t_filed / t_bound on it (#2235)
FLEET_PRETRUST_NODE_MAX_AGE        knob: how old (s, default 86400) the proxy's cached hub trust word may be for the trusted-node wide pre-trust (#2282)
FLEET_TIMING_READY_SECS            knob: how long a start's executor watches its window for t_ready (fleet_control.py, 120; 0 = never; issue #2238)
FLEET_CRED_PROXY_START_SECS        knob: how long `fleet-cred-proxy.sh ensure` waits for the proxy to come up (30)
FLEET_CRED_PROXY_WATCH_SECS        knob: how often the proxy launcher looks at its proxy — a dead one is restarted on the next look (2, #1975)
FLEET_CRED_ROLLOUT_WAIT            knob: how long `fleet cred-proxy enable|disable` waits for the proxy to come up / go down (75 s, #2134)
FLEET_CRED_ROLLOUT_DAEMON          seam: fleet-cred-rollout sandbox — a command run instead of the daemon step (#2134)
FLEET_CRED_ROLLOUT_PROCS           seam: fleet-cred-rollout sandbox — a file of `<argv0>\t<argv+env>` rows instead of the process table (#2134)
FLEET_CRED_ROLLOUT_SYNC            seam: fleet-cred-rollout sandbox — the fleet-sync-logins.sh --all-logins runs (#2134)
FLEET_CRED_ROLLOUT_CREDSEP         seam: fleet-cred-rollout sandbox — the fleet-credsep.sh `--machine` runs (#2217)
FLEET_CRED_SHARED_PORT             knob: the machine's shared credential proxy's fixed 127.0.0.1 port (18923; read at `machine install`, #2217)
FLEET_CRED_SHARED_TEST             seam: the shared proxy's sandbox — honour a control call's claimed peer uid (set only by fleet-credsep-launch.py under FLEET_CREDSEP_TEST, #2217)
FLEET_CRED_TEST_PEER_UID           seam: the shared proxy's sandbox — the peer uid a control call claims (#2217)
FLEET_CRED_AS                      env handoff: root at the shared proxy's control socket names the login it acts for (#2217)
FLEET_CREDSEP_PW                   seam: fleet-credsep sandbox — `name:uid:gid:home` rows instead of the password database (#2217)
FLEET_CRED_CODEX_HOMES             path: where the proxy reads Codex account homes (~/.codex-accounts); fleet-session-cred.sh maps a home to its label by it (#1970/#1972)
FLEET_CRED_QUOTA_PUSH              handoff: what the proxy runs after a fresh quota reading — fleet-cred-proxy.sh points it at fleet-proxy-quota.sh; empty = off (#1978)
FLEET_CRED_QUOTA_PUSH_SECS         knob: the proxy's debounce before that push (2 s, #1978)
FLEET_RL_PROXY_FRESH               knob: how long a proxy quota stamp holds against the status line and the mod (300 s; statusline.sh reads the env only, #1978)
FLEET_CRED_SID                     handoff: the per-launch credential-proxy session id fleet-session-wrap.sh hands the launcher (#1972)
FLEET_CREDS_IMPORT_NO_HOLDER       handoff: `fleet account add` tells fleet-creds-import.sh no Codex home here holds the account, so no «stop refreshing» reminder (#2084)
FLEET_DRILL_INVITE                 handoff: the drill's approve code, fleet-onboard-drill.sh → fleet-drill.sh approve (never an argv, #2010)
FLEET_DRILL_LOGIN_REMOVE           seam: the login-remove script fleet-onboard-drill.sh tears down with (selftest sandbox, #2010)
FLEET_CRED_CTL_DIR                 handoff: separated (#1971) — the run dir of the role account's proxy (ctl.sock, port); fleet-cred-proxy.sh sets it for its ctl client
FLEET_CREDSEP_DAEMON_DIR           seam: fleet-credsep sandbox — where the proxy/agent service definitions are written (/Library/LaunchDaemons, /etc/systemd/system)
FLEET_CREDSEP_LIB                  seam: fleet-credsep sandbox — the root-owned code copy the role account runs
FLEET_CREDSEP_LOG_BASE             seam: fleet-credsep sandbox — the proxy's log dir (/var/log/fleet-cred)
FLEET_CREDSEP_ROLE                 seam: fleet-credsep sandbox — an EXISTING user standing in for the role account (never created/deleted)
FLEET_CREDSEP_ROOT_BASE            seam: fleet-credsep sandbox — the store's base (/var/db/fleet-cred)
FLEET_CREDSEP_RUN_BASE             seam: fleet-credsep sandbox — the proxy's run dir base (/var/run/fleet-cred)
FLEET_CREDSEP_SUDO                 seam: fleet-credsep — the privilege prefix (default `sudo -n`; empty = run directly, the sandbox)
FLEET_CREDSEP_SVC                  seam: fleet-credsep sandbox — 0 = print launchctl/systemctl commands instead of running them
FLEET_CREDSEP_TEST                 seam: fleet-credsep sandbox — allow a non-root install/launch into the sandbox paths
FLEET_CRED_RELAY_RECHECK_SECS      knob: how often the proxy launcher re-checks / re-mints its relay pass (1800, #1974)
FLEET_CRED_RELAY_TOKEN             handoff: a hand-set relay pass, read from secrets.env only — never a setting; unset = the one fleet-relay-cred.sh mints (#1970, #1974)
FLEET_DRILL_AGENT_SECS             knob: fleet-onboard-drill.sh's wait for the session to read the screenshot (300 s, #2139)
FLEET_DRILL_NODE_BIN               knob: the session login's fleet bin/ fleet-onboard-drill.sh restarts it with (default ~<login>/.claude/fleet/bin, #2139)
FLEET_DRILL_OPENING_SECS           knob: fleet-onboard-drill.sh's wait while the hub opens the login (360 s, #2069)
FLEET_DRILL_POLL_SECS              knob: how often fleet-onboard-drill.sh reads its pane (2 s)
FLEET_DRILL_REMOVE_SECS            knob: fleet-onboard-drill.sh's wait while the hub closes the drill person's login (600 s, #2139)
FLEET_DRILL_RETIRE_CMD             seam: the command fleet-onboard-drill.sh retires a drill node with when fleet node leave did not (#1928)
FLEET_DRILL_SCAN_SECS              knob: how long fleet-onboard-drill.sh waits for the QR scan (600 s, the code's life)
FLEET_DRILL_STEP_SECS              knob: fleet-onboard-drill.sh's wait for any other step (120 s)
FLEET_DRILL_TIMEOUT                knob: fleet-onboard-drill.sh's wait for the download (900 s)
FLEET_HUB_TOKEN                    handoff: a viewer token from the environment (the client's hub token; fleet-onboard-drill.sh's revoke)
FLEET_INSTALL_VERSION              seam: the version a pinned FLEET_INSTALL_SRC is (the client's no-hub stage passes stable's commit; set = .client-version written, #1805)
FLEET_ITERM_DIR                    path: where the iTerm2 profile `fleet` is written (fleet-iterm-profile.py; selftests' sandbox, #1903)
FLEET_ITERM_KEYS                   knob: 0 removes the iTerm2 ⌘-key profile and never switches into it (fleet-shell.sh / fleet-iterm-profile.py, #1903)
FLEET_ROWS_UNFOLD                  handoff: 1 = the rows producer skips its fold filters — ⌘P / the switch history list every session (fleet-quickopen.py, #1903)
FLEET_ROWS_TEST                    handoff: 1 = the rows producer lists the test identity's sessions it otherwise hides — `fleet ls` / `fleet close --test` (fleet-session-cli.py, #2505)
FLEET_CLIENT_IDENTITY              handoff: test = the client is the TEST identity (`fleet --test-identity`, #1931); its scratch is marked and a NO_ATTACH placement closed at once (fleet-client-place.sh, fleet-shell.sh, #2505)
FLEET_SIDEBAR_HOST                 seam: this computer's hostname for the sidebar's @本机 mark and the proxy title (fleet-sidebar.py, fleet-remote-view.sh, #1780)
FLEET_CLIENT_BADGE_TTL             knob: seconds between the badge's where reads (fleet-client-badge.sh, 10, #1779)
FLEET_CLIENT_BADGE_WHERE_CMD       seam: the where read fleet-client-badge.sh runs (default fleet-client-where.sh --json, #1779)
FLEET_CLIENT_WHERE_CMD             seam: the hub read fleet-client-where.sh runs (default python3 fleet-client-lease.py where; the selftest swaps in a file, #1716)
FLEET_CLIENT_XTVERSION             knob: 0 = never ask the terminal its name at client start (fleet-client-lease.py, 1, #1716)
FLEET_CLEANUP_LEASE_TTL            knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-cleanup-daemon.sh)
FLEET_CODEX_ACCOUNT                handoff: the codex account a launch was assigned
FLEET_CODEX_MANAGED                handoff: marks a codex launch as fleet-managed
FLEET_CODEX_PROFILE                handoff: an explicit codex profile for this launch
FLEET_CODEX_READY_CHECK            knob: 0 skips the Codex-login check before a Codex spawn (fleet-lib.sh fleet_codex_ready, #2562)
FLEET_CODEX_READY_CMD              seam: prints `ccquota codex list` instead of running it (fleet_codex_ready, #2562)
FLEET_COLLECT_QUOTAWATCH           knob: auto|never — whether the collector runs the quotawatch phase inline
FLEET_COMPACT_SEND_GRACE           knob: seconds fleet-compact-send.sh waits for the Stop hook to return before its idle check (2)
FLEET_COMPACT_RESUME_GRACE         knob: seconds fleet-compact-resume.sh waits after the restore before its idle check (3)
FLEET_COMPACT_RESUME_TIMEOUT       knob: how long fleet-compact-resume.sh holds for an untyped-at pane before giving up (90)
FLEET_COMPACT_RESUME_WATCH         knob: how long fleet-compact-resume.sh watches a stale `working` for the pane to settle before skip:stale (600, #1572)
FLEET_COMPACT_SEND_TIMEOUT         knob: how long fleet-compact-send.sh holds for an idle, untyped-at pane before giving up (90)
FLEET_CONFIG_SHOW_INTERNAL         knob: fcfg_table lists @tier=internal rows too (#1101) — a per-call switch, not a conf setting
